===Proper noun===
'''Threadneedle Street'''
#{{London}} a [[street]] in the [[City]], running from [[Poultry]] and [[Lombard Street]] to [[Bishopsgate]]; the site of the [[Bank of England]]
# {{UK|finance}} The [[w:Bank of England|Bank of England (at Wikipedia)]].
#:* '''2008''' Thursday March 6, ''Eddie George defends role of FSA in Northern Rock crisis'', in [[w:The Guardian|The Guardian]]
#::* George, known as Steady Eddie during his 10 years in charge at '''Threadneedle Street''', said critics who attacked the Financial Services Authority were also wide of the mark.
#:* '''2008''' February 10, ''Couture hits the high street'', by Maurice Chittenden in [[w:The Sunday Times|The Sunday Times]]
#::* Osman Yousefzada, who exhibits his own label today, also designs for Mango. He was a City banker before swapping '''Threadneedle Street''' for needle and thread.